# UI theming (clients/web)

Never hardcode colors (`#hex`, `rgb()`, `bg-white`, `text-gray-900`, `border-slate-200`, SVG `fill="#…"`). Use semantic Tailwind tokens mapped from CSS variables in `src/styles/theme.css` / `src/config/theme.ts`: `background`, `foreground`, `surface`, `border`, `muted`, `primary`, `accent`, `ring`, `danger`, `success`, `info`, `chat-*`, `citation`, `sidebar`, `code`.

Brand (primary/accent) changes are token-only. Add a named theme by adding a palette in `src/config/theme.ts` (then regenerate/sync `theme.css`); it must appear in `ThemeToggle` via config, not one-off class names.

Every new component must be checked in **light and dark** (and system). Run `make web-test-theme` when changing tokens.
